WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.558
A week has seven days. A
year has twelve months.

2
00:00:07.778 --> 00:00:11.214
And a clock tells you
the time, with two hands.

3
00:00:11.714 --> 00:00:14.965
The days of the week always
come round in the same order.

4
00:00:15.185 --> 00:00:18.157
Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday,
Thursday, Friday.

5
00:00:18.377 --> 00:00:21.535
Then Saturday, and then
Sunday. That is seven days.

6
00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:25.656
After Sunday the week starts
again at Monday, round and round.

7
00:00:25.876 --> 00:00:30.706
The day after Wednesday is Thursday.
The day before Saturday is Friday.

8
00:00:31.206 --> 00:00:34.782
A year is made of twelve months.
They always come in this order.

9
00:00:35.002 --> 00:00:38.206
January, February,
March, April, May, June.

10
00:00:38.426 --> 00:00:42.049
July, August, September,
October, November, December.

11
00:00:42.269 --> 00:00:45.566
The year starts at January
and it ends at December.

12
00:00:45.786 --> 00:00:49.455
Hodan was born in the first
month. That month is January.

13
00:00:49.955 --> 00:00:54.227
Some things take a very short
time. Some take a very long time.

14
00:00:54.447 --> 00:00:57.744
One clap takes about a
second. That is the shortest.

15
00:00:57.964 --> 00:01:01.215
Sixty seconds make one
minute. A minute is longer.

16
00:01:01.435 --> 00:01:05.382
One lesson at school lasts about
an hour. That is sixty minutes.

17
00:01:05.602 --> 00:01:09.828
A day is one whole sleep to the
next sleep. That is much longer.

18
00:01:10.048 --> 00:01:13.578
A week is seven days. That
is the longest one here.

19
00:01:14.078 --> 00:01:17.468
A clock has two hands.
They do two different jobs.

20
00:01:17.688 --> 00:01:21.125
The short hand is the hour
hand. It tells you the hour.

21
00:01:21.345 --> 00:01:24.874
The long hand tells you how
far through the hour you are.

22
00:01:25.094 --> 00:01:28.809
Always look for the short
hand first, every single time.

23
00:01:29.029 --> 00:01:32.744
The long hand is bigger,
but it never tells the hour.

24
00:01:33.244 --> 00:01:36.449
At o'clock, the long hand
points straight up to twelve.

25
00:01:36.669 --> 00:01:40.012
Here the short hand is on the
three. It is three o'clock.

26
00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:43.901
School starts at eight o'clock.
The short hand points to eight.

27
00:01:44.121 --> 00:01:47.883
At half past, the long hand
points straight down to six.

28
00:01:48.103 --> 00:01:51.632
Now the short hand sits between
two numbers on the face.

29
00:01:51.852 --> 00:01:55.614
It is between three and four.
So it is half past three.

30
00:01:56.114 --> 00:01:59.643
Seven days make a week.
Twelve months make a year.

31
00:01:59.863 --> 00:02:03.718
A second is short. A whole year
is long. Pick the right word.

32
00:02:03.938 --> 00:02:07.699
Long hand up is o'clock.
Long hand down is half past.

33
00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:11.449
And the short hand always
tells you the hour, every time.
